id="lab-auto" type="checkbox" ${labAutoCombo?'checked':''} ${!labActive||livePractice?'disabled':''}> Auto chain in practice · same combat rules</label><label><input id="lab-stamina" type="checkbox" ${labUnlimitedStamina?'checked':''} ${!labActive||livePractice?'disabled':''}> Unlimited practice stamina</label><label><input id="lab-targets" type="checkbox" ${labInfiniteTargets?'checked':''} ${!labActive||livePractice?'disabled':''}> Indestructible practice dummy</label><p>Measurement runs turn both off. They never apply in the campaign.</p></details><button id="lab-equipment" ${!labActive?'disabled':''}>Equipment · preview, compare & practice</button><p>Practice uses your selected lab loadout. Starting the nine-scenario suite resets your lab loadout to the unchanged survey-staff baseline; matched equipment comparisons are available in the equipment workbench.</p><h3>LIVE SENTRY PRACTICE</h3><p>A real quadruped and nearby solid wall, using the same warning, guard, low-strike and staff rules. Practice health and costs are separate from your campaign. Face the sentry with movement, read the amber warning, then sidestep or jump; G guards one timed front contact. Q/R only orbit the camera. No result here is an automatic visual pass.</p><button id="lab-live-reset" ${!labActive||transitioning||!physicsReady?'disabled':''}>${livePractice?'Reset live sentry · fresh attempt':'Start live sentry practice'}</button><div class="row"><button id="lab-live-resume" ${!livePractice||!['paused','ready'].includes(livePractice.status)?'disabled':''}>Resume live practice</button><button id="lab-live-stop" ${!livePractice?'disabled':''}>Stop · return to course</button></div><p id="lab-live-status"></p><div class="row"><button id="lab-live-capture" ${!livePractice||!['active','paused','ready'].includes(livePractice.status)?'disabled':''}>Capture next 2 seconds</button><button id="lab-live-export" ${!liveRecording?'disabled':''}>Export practice trace</button></div><p>Reset replaces the disposable attempt. Menus pause it; missed physics steps require Resume or Reset. Suit or sentry defeat requires Reset. Change equipment/tuning before starting. Unlimited stamina, indestructible dummy and auto-chain aids do not apply.</p><h3>REPEATABLE MEASUREMENT</h3><p>The physics worker schedules every scripted input on its own fixed clock, including when rendering stalls. Each case rebuilds a fresh physics world and resets character, targets, combo, camera and inputs. One second / 60 simulation steps of warmup is excluded. Automated checks use collision-resolved snapshots. Visual quality needs your review below.</p><label for="lab-iterations">Identical full-suite runs</label><select id="lab-iterations"><option value="1">1 run · about 35 seconds</option><option value="3">3 runs · about 2 minutes</option><option value="5">5 runs · about 3 minutes</option></select><button id="lab-run" ${!labActive||transitioning?'disabled':''}>Run all nine scenarios</button><p>Keep this tab focused. Menus, app switching, resize, backgrounding or leaving the lab interrupt the measurement; incomplete runs are never marked passed.</p></section><section data-lab-page="systems" hidden><h3>WORLD SYSTEM SCENARIOS</h3><p>These open separate, disposable production models. They are fast-forward tests, not playable terrain. Seed, target, rainfall, travel model and fixed-step playback are editable there; each has reset, balances, actions and export/replay.</p><div class="lab-scenario-grid"><a class="lab-scenario-link" href="./system-workbench.html?seed=${state.seed}&amp;system=settlement" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>From-zero settlement ↗</strong><span>Freight, construction, water, farming and meals together</span></a><a class="lab-scenario-link" href="./system-workbench.html?seed=${state.seed}&amp;system=water" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Rain & drought ↗</strong><span>Collector storage, spillage and thirsty residents</span></a><a class="lab-scenario-link" href="./system-workbench.html?seed=${state.seed}&amp;system=trade" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Freight & wet roads ↗</strong><span>Finite extraction, road repair and store construction</span></a><a class="lab-scenario-link" href="./system-workbench.html?seed=${state.seed}&amp;system=food" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Farm to meals ↗</strong><span>Crop water, growth, pantry, hunger and stewardship</span></a><a class="lab-scenario-link" href="./system-workbench.html?seed=${state.seed}&amp;system=food&amp;irrigation=canister" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Emergency irrigation ↗</strong><span>One earned canister, one real manual use</span></a></div><h3>PROGRESSION & RESOURCES</h3><p>AXIOM has no XP or level system. Progression uses earned materials, community renown, construction and stewardship. Reward budgets and resource ledgers are replay-validated, so arbitrary XP, reward or stock multipliers are not exposed. Run world systems below to test earned rewards, manufacture, ecology, barter and water requests; use from-zero settlement for the regional chain.</p><h3>REPEATABLE WORLD SYSTEM CHECKS</h3><p>Disposable production-model checks cover enemy warning/counterplay, all three flood-route solutions, water-supported manufacture, garden recipes, cave delivery, guard timing, a fixed-seed household-barter repair counterfactual and two consumption-driven request episodes. These do not certify pixels, internet play or frame rate.</p><h3>REGIONAL FOOD LOOP</h3><button id="regional-food-lab">Run disposable farm-to-meal checks</button><button id="regional-food-export" ${regionalFoodReport?'':'disabled'}>Export food report</button><p id="regional-food-lab-status">New collector overflow → seed → crop → reserved food → local carrier → pantry → meals. Independent worlds never change your campaign.</p><h3>REGIONAL FREIGHT LOOP</h3><button id="regional-trade-lab">Run disposable freight-route checks</button><button id="regional-trade-export" ${regionalTradeReport?'':'disabled'}>Export freight report</button><p id="regional-trade-lab-status">Finite extraction → reserved cargo → real road travel → repair → delivery → freight-store construction. These disposable checks never change your campaign.</p><h3>REGIONAL SETTLEMENT LOOP</h3><button id="regional-supply-lab">Run disposable supply-loop checks</button><button id="regional-supply-export" ${regionalSupplyReport?'':'disabled'}>Export settlement report</button><p id="regional-supply-lab-status">Gather → deliver → construction → resident water benefit → leave, return and save. Uses independent deterministic worlds and real material IDs; it does not certify rendered visuals or internet latency.</p><h3>WILDERNESS COLLISION</h3><div class="row"><button id="wilderness-probes">Run isolated solid probes</button><button id="wilderness-probes-export">Export collision report</button></div><button id="wilderness-outlines">Toggle wilderness solid outlines</button><p id="wilderness-probes-status">Repeated real-worker tree and rock approaches, both saved generations. Campaign data stays untouched; rendered appearance needs your review.</p><button id="lab-systems">Run world systems · repeated checks</button><button id="lab-systems-export" ${systemsReport?'':'disabled'}>Export world systems report</button><p id="lab-systems-summary"></p></section><section data-lab-page="inspect" hidden><h3>PROCEDURAL GENERATION</h3><div class="row"><button id="lab-procedural" ${labActive?'disabled':''}>Seed & recipe inspector</button><button id="lab-plans" ${labActive?'disabled':''}>Valley & vault plans</button></div><p>${labActive?'Return to campaign first to use these two read-only in-game inspectors. The separate system workbench remains available while the lab is open. ':''}Preview another seed, recipe or domain and inspect real constraints, geometry and manifests. Compile regenerates only the preview. Saved worlds keep their pinned generation. Terrain amplitude, room counts, enemy counts and arbitrary scripts are not currently supported controls.</p><h3>RENDERED VISUAL TOOLS</h3><p><a href="./visual-review.html?subject=animation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open isolated animation inspector</a> · play, scrub and frame-step production physics/rig snapshots; capture PNG and pose/contact JSON without booting this world. Actual captured images are never automatic visual approval.</p><p>Contact animation clips include wall pressure, crate push/pull and ledge mantle. These are fixed worker replays you can scrub, not editable campaign props.</p><button id="lab-capture-run" ${!labActive||transitioning?'disabled':''}>Capture selected station · real worker replay</button><div class="row"><button id="lab-capture-png">Download captured contact sheet</button><button id="lab-capture-json">Download capture evidence</button></div><p id="capture-status"></p></section><section data-lab-page="tuning" hidden><h3>SESSION TUNING</h3><p>Edit a draft, then Apply. Closing this panel discards unapplied edits. Ordinary campaign mechanics use release defaults. Live sentry settings are latched: stop the attempt before applying, then start a fresh attempt.</p><label for="lab-quick-preset">Ready-to-test draft</label><select id="lab-quick-preset"><option value="">Choose a setup…</option>${Object.entries(LAB_QUICK_PRESETS).map(([id,p])=>`<option value="${id}">${p.label}</option>`).join('')}</select><label for="lab-filter">Find a control</label><input id="lab-filter" type="search" placeholder="Damage, gravity, camera…"><p id="lab-draft-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Applied values shown · no pending changes</p><fieldset id="lab-tuning-fields" ${livePractice||coop.active||coopPending||coop.status==='connecting'?'disabled':''}>${tuningHTML(labTuning)}</fieldset><div class="lab-apply-bar"><button id="lab-apply">Apply draft to lab</button><button id="lab-cancel-draft">Discard draft</button><button id="lab-defaults">Reset all draft values</button></div><p>Movement and camera take effect after Apply in the paused lab. Staff changes affect the next accepted strike. Sentry damage takes effect on its next reset. A modified setup may fail a release-baseline measurement; that is useful feedback.</p><div class="row"><button id="lab-save-preset">Save applied device preset</button><button id="lab-load-preset">Load device preset into draft</button></div><p>Explicit save/load only. Presets never load automatically and never write a campaign slot.</p><label><input id="lab-reduced" type="checkbox" ${reducedMotion?'checked':''}> Reduced motion · no impact hold or camera shake</label></section><section data-lab-page="reports" hidden><h3>STARTUP DIAGNOSTICS</h3><p>Inspect or copy the latest startup report. Tests apply once after a full reload from the last saved checkpoint; unsaved play is not carried into the test. They never alter a save or persist a bad setting.</p><button id="lab-startup-report">Open startup report</button><label for="lab-startup-test">Next startup scenario</label><select id="lab-startup-test">${STARTUP_TESTS.map(test=>`<option value="${test.id}">${test.label}</option>`).join('')}</select><p id="lab-startup-test-effect"></p><button id="lab-startup-run" ${coop.active||coopPending?'disabled':''}>Reload from saved checkpoint &amp; test</button><h3>SHARE A REPRODUCIBLE TEST</h3><p>Export the applied setup or feedback with build, seed, scenario, settings and available measured evidence. No account or room tokens are included. Import accepts only bounded lab presets and stages a draft; it never starts a test or changes world saves.</p><div class="row"><button id="lab-preset-export">Export applied preset</button><button id="lab-feedback-export">Export feedback report</button><button id="lab-copy">Copy prepared JSON</button></div><label for="lab-portable">Preset / feedback JSON · copy fallback</label><textarea id="lab-portable" rows="7" maxlength="24000" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Export prepares readable text here. Paste a lab preset here to import."></textar